From: Nura rc4 series <rc4@nura.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: listen for Source_Capabilities during the sink hard-reset wait

After a Hard Reset in the sink role, tcpm disables PD RX in
HARD_RESET_START and only re-enables it in SNK_WAIT_CAPABILITIES, after
SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_OFF has waited PD_T_SAFE_0V (650 ms) for VBUS to drop.

A self-powered USB-C dock keeps VBUS up across the Hard Reset and
resends Source_Capabilities at once, then does not retry. Its messages hit
the PM8150B PD PHY while RX is off and are discarded (msg-rx-discarded:
exactly one per attach plus one per hard reset; msg-rx stays 0, even with
sink-wait-cap-time-ms raised to 2000), so every attach ends without a
contract and DisplayPort never starts. USB-PD wall chargers, which wait
longer, are unaffected.

Enable PD RX (and restart the message counters) when entering
SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_OFF. If Source_Capabilities arrive in
SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_OFF or SNK_HARD_RESET_WAIT_VBUS, finish the hard reset
the way SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_ON does and go straight to
SNK_NEGOTIATE_CAPABILITIES, so the Request goes out within tSenderResponse
instead of the generic path turning the message into a soft reset.

Nura-Category: usb-pd
Nura-Origin: guacamole powered-dock tcpm logs 2026-11-15 (.work/pd-wait620, .work/pd-wait2000)
Upstream-Status: candidate
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -3252,6 +3252,23 @@
 			port->ams = POWER_NEGOTIATION;
 			port->in_ams = true;
 			tcpm_set_state(port, SNK_NEGOTIATE_CAPABILITIES, 0);
+		} else if (port->state == SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_OFF ||
+			   port->state == SNK_HARD_RESET_WAIT_VBUS) {
+			/*
+			 * The source recovered from our Hard Reset without
+			 * dropping VBUS (see SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_OFF). Finish
+			 * the reset as SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_ON would and answer
+			 * within tSenderResponse instead of soft-resetting.
+			 */
+			if (port->ams == HARD_RESET)
+				tcpm_ams_finish(port);
+			tcpm_set_attached_state(port, true);
+			tcpm_set_auto_vbus_discharge_threshold(port, TYPEC_PWR_MODE_USB,
+							       false, VSAFE5V);
+			port->explicit_contract = false;
+			port->ams = POWER_NEGOTIATION;
+			port->in_ams = true;
+			tcpm_set_state(port, SNK_NEGOTIATE_CAPABILITIES, 0);
 		} else {
 			if (port->ams == GET_SOURCE_CAPABILITIES)
 				tcpm_ams_finish(port);
@@ -5506,6 +5523,20 @@
 		tcpm_set_roles(port, port->self_powered, TYPEC_STATE_USB, TYPEC_SINK,
 			       tcpm_data_role_for_sink(port));
 		/*
+		 * Some sources (seen: a self-powered USB-C dock) keep VBUS up
+		 * across a Hard Reset and resend Source_Capabilities at once,
+		 * long before PD_T_SAFE_0V expires. With PD RX still disabled
+		 * since HARD_RESET_START the PHY discards them and the source
+		 * does not retry, so every attach ends without a contract.
+		 * Listen during the wait; the message counters restart after a
+		 * Hard Reset.
+		 */
+		if (port->pd_supported) {
+			port->message_id = 0;
+			port->rx_msgid = -1;
+			port->tcpc->set_pd_rx(port->tcpc, true);
+		}
+		/*
 		 * VBUS may or may not toggle, depending on the adapter.
 		 * If it doesn't toggle, transition to SNK_HARD_RESET_SINK_ON
 		 * directly after timeout.
